1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:00,940
If this sea slug

2
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:02,290
cuts off its own HEAD…

3
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,260
that head can keep CRAWLING.

4
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:05,740
And its headless BODY?

5
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,240
It keeps MOVING too.

6
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,700
You see, there’s a weak spot

7
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:09,980
just behind its head.

8
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,040
When it breaks apart,

9
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,960
even its HEART stays behind.

10
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,020
Scientists think it may be

11
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:15,060
escaping PARASITES

12
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,280
in its old body.

13
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:16,820
But the head

14
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,160
starts eating algae…

15
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,280
and about a week later,

16
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,200
a NEW HEART starts BEATING.

17
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,720
Then, over the next few weeks,

18
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:25,000
an ENTIRE NEW BODY grows back.

19
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,280
And one of these sea slugs

20
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,667
actually did it… TWICE.

